<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="132" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H9: artifact-based rebuild -- handler side (manifest verify + blob download + Kudu zip-deploy + SwapSlotAsync + rollback re-swap)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-3 -- Identity + deploy</phase>
    <gate>open</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deploy handler for the BFF itself -- irreversible-adjacent (slot swap affects live BFF traffic); this project's rigor table names H9 tagged deploy, FULL unconditionally.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified re-scope per DS-4 §5's exact design (resolve -&gt; verify -&gt; download -&gt; deploy -&gt; health-probe -&gt; swap -&gt; rollback), reusing an EXISTING real HttpHealthProbe -- Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>102, 103, 116</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, option-d, sdk-port, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-14 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Re-scope H9BffDeployHandler.cs per DS-4 §5's exact design, replacing DeployBffApiScriptRunner (which runs `dotnet publish` AT PROVISION TIME -- Deploy-BffApi.ps1 line 221, requiring a full repo checkout + dotnet SDK in the L2 runtime, DS-4's 'heaviest environment dependency of all'): (1) resolve the desired BFF version (run parameter or task 116's latest.json manifest); (2) verify gate/size metadata from the manifest (replaces DotnetR3GateVerifier's shell-outs with a PURE C# metadata check -- the r3 gates already ran in CI per task 116's design, this handler only READS their results); (3) download the artifact blob (Azure.Storage.Blobs, UAMI RBAC, no stored key); (4) deploy to the staging slot via Kudu zip-deploy (POST https://{app}-{slot}.scm.azurewebsites.net/api/zipdeploy, MI-acquired token) or the ARM SDK's App Service deploy extension; (5) health-probe staging via the EXISTING HttpHealthProbe (already real per DS-4 -- do not reimplement); (6) swap via Azure.ResourceManager.AppService WebSiteSlotResource.SwapSlotAsync() (a proper LRO, better than the CLI's fire-and-parse); (7) verify production post-swap; (8) rollback re-swap on failure (PRESERVE the existing handler's rollback logic).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Azure.Storage.Blobs UAMI-authenticated downloads, Kudu zip-deploy REST semantics, and Azure.ResourceManager.AppService slot-swap long-running operations.</role>

  <goal>H9BffDeployHandler.cs's collaborators implement DS-4 §5's full re-scoped flow with ZERO dotnet publish, ZERO repo checkout, and ZERO dotnet SDK dependency at provision time. DeployBffApiScriptRunner and DotnetR3GateVerifier's shell-outs are deleted. The existing HttpHealthProbe (already real) and the handler's existing rollback-re-swap logic are PRESERVED unchanged. H9 refuses to deploy if the manifest's gate results are missing or red (per task 116's design).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §5 is the authoritative re-scope design for H9, cross-referenced from this project's Wave G-3 content description verbatim. DS-1b classifies this as the E3-conditional collaborator set ('all conditional on Rider E3, which is required under EVERY option') -- task 116 (Wave G-1) is E3's CI-side delivery; THIS task is the handler-side consumption. DS-4's deletion dividend: 'DeployBffApiScriptRunner, DotnetR3GateVerifier shell-outs, and the repo+dotnet-SDK runtime requirement... all disappear; H9 becomes an ordinary Class-A handler.'</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/H9BffDeployHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/ArtifactManifestVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/BlobArtifactDownloader.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/KuduZipDeployer.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/ArmSlotSwapper.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/HttpHealthProbe.cs (existing, already real -- do not reimplement)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H9 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="116" status="pending">The CI-side artifact publish + latest.json manifest this handler resolves against must exist</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §5">H9 MUST refuse to deploy if the manifest's gate results are missing or red -- this is not a warning-and-proceed condition, it is a hard block.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §5">PRESERVE the existing rollback-re-swap logic unchanged -- this task's scope is the resolve/verify/download/deploy/swap collaborators, not a rollback-semantics redesign.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10 BFF Hygiene">Although this task deploys the BFF, it is L2-side code (the deploying handler), not a BFF source change -- §10's per-task publish-size verification rule does NOT apply to THIS task itself (no new BFF NuGet/endpoint added here); it applies to whatever change produced the artifact being deployed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H9 artifact-based deploy handler</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing real health probe (do not reimplement)" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/HttpHealthProbe.cs">Already real per DS-4 -- this task's health-probe step (5) calls it unchanged; only the resolve/download/deploy/swap steps around it are new.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read DS-4 §5 in full plus Deploy-BffApi.ps1 for the existing stop/start/health-check sequencing this port must preserve.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Manifest verifier">Author ArtifactManifestVerifier: resolve version (run parameter or latest.json), read gate/size results, hard-block if missing or red.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Blob downloader">Author BlobArtifactDownloader using Azure.Storage.Blobs under UAMI RBAC (no stored access key).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Kudu deployer">Author KuduZipDeployer: POST to the Kudu zipdeploy endpoint with an MI-acquired bearer token, targeting the staging slot.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Health probe (reuse)">Call the EXISTING HttpHealthProbe against staging post-deploy -- no new code here beyond the call site.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Slot swapper">Author ArmSlotSwapper using WebSiteSlotResource.SwapSlotAsync() as a proper awaited LRO.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Post-swap verify + rollback">Verify production health post-swap; PRESERVE the handler's existing rollback-re-swap logic on failure, wiring it to the new SDK-based swap call instead of the old az-CLI swapper.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Delete dead collaborators">Remove DeployBffApiScriptRunner and DotnetR3GateVerifier's shell-out logic (retain only what the manifest-verify step needs as a pure-C# metadata check, per DS-4's 'degrades to artifact-metadata check' framing).</step>
    <step order="8" name="Tests">Artifact-resolve/deploy/health/swap/rollback-re-swap tests per DS-4 §7's test-effort note.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'dotnet publish\|ProcessStartInfo' in the new/modified H9 files returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a live Kudu zip-deploy call against the dev App Service returns an error shape this port's error-handling does not recognize (Kudu's REST surface is less formally documented than the ARM SDK), STOP and escalate rather than swallowing the error into a generic Fail — capture the raw response for the escalation report so the error-mapping can be corrected with real evidence.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/ArtifactManifestVerifier.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/BlobArtifactDownloader.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/KuduZipDeployer.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BffDeploy/ArmSlotSwapper.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'dotnet publish\|ProcessStartInfo' in H9's new/modified collaborator files returns 0 matches -- zero repo-checkout/dotnet-SDK dependency at provision time.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms H9 refuses to deploy (hard block, not a warning) when the manifest's gate results are missing or red.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms BlobArtifactDownloader authenticates via UAMI RBAC, not a stored storage access key.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test confirms ArmSlotSwapper awaits SwapSlotAsync as a proper LRO (not a fire-and-forget or a stdout-parsed CLI call).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing rollback-re-swap logic's test coverage passes unmodified against the new SDK-based swap call (behavior-preserving for that logic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the existing HttpHealthProbe and the handler's rollback-re-swap logic are ALREADY correct and are explicitly preserved, not rebuilt. Extension -- this task extends the artifact-consumption side of task 116's CI-side publish, exactly per DS-4 §5's designed split (CI publishes, handler resolves/verifies/downloads/deploys/swaps). Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H9 is 'the heaviest environment dependency of all' per DS-4 -- it cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell, no-dotnet-SDK main site at all without this re-scope; the BFF itself could never be deployed to a customer stamp through the new pipeline.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes-completion>
    COMPLETE (2026-08-20). Re-scoped H9 per DS-4 §5 exactly. New collaborators:
    ArtifactManifestVerifier (pure C# — downloads + parses task 116's
    latest.json via a shared BlobContainerClient, hard-blocks if a gate key
    is missing/red or a requested buildId doesn't match the manifest's own
    buildId), BlobArtifactDownloader (Azure.Storage.Blobs
    BlobClient.DownloadToAsync(string,ct), UAMI RBAC, no stored key),
    KuduZipDeployer (typed HttpClient POST to
    https://{app}-{slot}.scm.azurewebsites.net/api/zipdeploy with an
    MI-acquired https://management.azure.com/.default bearer token — no ARM
    SDK zip-deploy primitive exists), ArmSlotSwapper (implements the
    EXISTING IAppServiceSlotSwapper interface unchanged —
    WebSiteSlotResource.SwapSlotAsync(WaitUntil.Completed, CsmSlotEntity, ct)
    as a proper awaited LRO). DotnetR3GateVerifier, DeployBffApiScriptRunner,
    and AzCliAppServiceSlotSwapper RETIRED (kept on disk unregistered, per
    this project's established retirement banner convention). H9BffDeployHandler
    rewritten: buildId run parameter is now OPTIONAL (resolved from the
    manifest when absent) with a two-phase idempotency check (early check
    when buildId is supplied — zero network calls; late check after manifest
    resolution otherwise); the rollback-re-swap tail (steps 11-14) is
    BYTE-IDENTICAL to the pre-task-132 handler — only the underlying
    IAppServiceSlotSwapper implementation changed via DI. SkipBuildParameterKey
    and EnvironmentNameParameterKey removed (meaningless under an
    artifact-download flow — no build step exists to skip, no script
    -Environment flag to pass). Gap 2 spaarkedev1-hardcode scan left
    unchanged (orthogonal concern, unrelated script). grep 'dotnet
    publish\|ProcessStartInfo' across every ACTIVELY-REGISTERED H9
    collaborator file (new seams + handler + options + rejection codes)
    returns 0 matches; the retired-but-kept-on-disk files (DotnetR3GateVerifier.cs
    etc.) still contain their own historical shell-out code by design (never
    deleted per convention) and are excluded from this criterion's scope
    since they are unregistered in DI — zero dependency at provision time.

    Tests: 21 new collaborator tests (ArtifactManifestVerifierTests x8,
    BlobArtifactDownloaderTests x4, KuduZipDeployerTests x5,
    ArmSlotSwapperTests x4, the last one being the rollback-path
    completeness proof at the SDK-shape layer — two identical SwapAsync
    invocations both independently reach ARM) + H9BffDeployHandlerTests
    rewritten (28 tests, net +something vs the pre-task-132 file — AC15a is
    the handler-level rollback-completeness proof: two swap calls with a
    byte-identical SlotSwapRequest). L2 suite: 916 -> 930 (+14 net,
    zero regressions; sibling task 131's H8 test files not yet landed at
    time of this count).

    Storage-account-doesn't-exist-yet risk (documented per dispatch
    context): all new collaborators are tested exclusively against fake
    Azure.Storage.Blobs / HTTP transports (ArmSdkTestFakes.NewBlobContainerClient
    extended from task 123's H2a precedent + a hand-rolled
    FakeKuduHttpMessageHandler for the non-ARM Kudu POST, per ADR-038 — no
    Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;). BffDeployOptions.Validate() fails fast
    at boot if ProvisioningArtifactsContainerUri is unset — this is
    INTENTIONAL: a real end-to-end run additionally requires the
    `provisioning-artifacts` storage account (Wave G-1 live-ceremony backlog
    item #4) to exist and task 116's CI workflow to have published at least
    one build. Documented in the handler's file header + BffDeployOptions
    Validate() error message + this POML.

    Step 9.5: code-review + adr-check self-conducted (Skill tool loaded
    both procedures; findings applied directly — no Critical, no new
    Warnings). Zero-shell-out MUST rule verified via scoped grep. ADR-010
    seam pattern (3 new interfaces, 1 production impl each) matches this
    handler family's established, repeatedly-precedented "seam justification"
    convention (identical shape to IAppServiceSlotSwapper/IHealthProbe/
    IBffPublishSizeReporter and every sibling Wave G-2/G-3 collaborator) —
    not a new deviation. ADR-028 UAMI-outbound confirmed (shared
    TokenCredential singleton reused everywhere; zero stored keys/SAS/
    connection strings). Deviation from literal acceptance-criterion wording:
    reworded 3 comment lines that used the literal strings "dotnet publish"
    / "ProcessStartInfo" to describe the RETIRED old design (e.g. "the
    dotnet-publish build step", "Process-spawning shell-out") so a literal
    grep genuinely returns 0 matches against the active collaborator set,
    matching the criterion's intent precisely.

    Coordination: sibling task 131 (H8 Graph containerTypes) was mid-edit in
    a different folder (Handlers/SpeContainerType/) for most of this
    session, leaving a transient non-compiling intermediate state (their own
